<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna `pow2select`: signed `x / 2^k` rounds toward zero, so gcc biases a
    negative x by 2^k - 1 and selects the biased value with a cmov, which
    lifts as a branch and a MULTIEQUAL: `v = x + 3; if (0 <= x) v = x;
    return v >> 2;`.  With the option on (the default) the shift is
    rewritten to `x / 4` when the branch provably sends every positive x to
    the unbiased input and every negative x to the biased one.

    Stage / sub-stage: P3 "simplification-quiescence", option
    `pow2select on|off`.

    The bytes are decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/pow2select.c
    built by gcc 15.3 at -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles (x86-64 SysV).
    near1 tests x > 5 and near3 biases by 7 before a shift by 2; neither is a
    division and both keep their select.  Pass 1 is the default, pass 2
    `option pow2select off`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401000">
f30f1efa85ff8d47030f49c7c1f802c3f30f1efa4885ff488d471f480f49c748c1f805c39066662e0f1f840000000000f30f1efa89fac1fa1fc1ea1d8d041783
